They say it's bad luck to squeeze behind the boulders.

Generally, the best thing to do is to throw things (or cast/zap spells
which cause damage but aren't striking) to kill the offending
creature.  You don't have to throw "real" weapons (unless it's a troll
or such that'll heal quicker than you can hurt it with rocks and rusty
helmets).

Except in pathological cases, the worst that'll get you is a minor
alignment ding (peaceful foo behind boulder) which you can quickly
recover from by killing just about any random few hostile creatures.

Bypassing the boulders is only smart if you 1) have an ironclad way to
repair your luck quickly and 2) know you can take on whatever is
behind the boulder (and whatever might spawn nearby) without most of
your armour or other inventory.

